            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0840" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9169 Bogotá: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-05T22:00:00-05:00">May 5, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 6—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>849. For FEA. Department’s telegram 583, April 29, 5 p.m. and 600, May 3.<anchor
                        n="67" xml:id="d788-f1"/> In spite of simplification program already in
                    effect third quarter import recommendation applications now total more than
                    12,000 with returns yet incomplete. This is considerably greater than any
                    previous quarter since the establishment of the Decentralization <pb facs="0841"
                        n="827" xml:id="pg827"/> Plan. A difficult personnel program has developed
                    for handling this large volume. It will not be practicable to effect quota
                    distributions on the basis of provisional figures equivalent to second quarter
                    amounts. If definite third quarter quotas can reach the mission by June 1 little
                    time will be lost. It is urged however that an indication be telegraphed at once
                    of probable categories to be eliminated from decentralization procedure on July
                    1 so that processing of the corresponding import recommendations may be
                    postponed awaiting your official confirmation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
